A `TODO` marks planned work. A `FIXME` marks broken behaviour and a `HACK` a
fragile workaround; both are debt, so either fix them or file them as a task in
[TASKS.md](TASKS.md). `BUG` marks a defect known to affect users and should
never be merged unresolved.

Write the tag in uppercase followed by a colon and an imperative description,
and cite an issue when one exists.
```
// TODO: implement retry logic (#42)
// FIXME: panics on empty input
```

{% if include_annotation_gate %}Never merge `FIXME`, `BUG`, or `HACK` into `main`. Convert them to a task or resolve them before merging.{% else %}Resolve `FIXME`, `BUG`, and `HACK` before merging, or convert them into a task; no CI check enforces this here.{% endif %}

